1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,200
Hey, what colors do you think Hori-senpai would like best?

2
00:00:05,420 --> 00:00:08,040
I've seen her wear red and pink accessories before,

3
00:00:08,160 --> 00:00:09,500
so maybe warmer colors?

4
00:00:09,860 --> 00:00:11,600
Bound to beat something blue or white, yeah?

5
00:00:13,340 --> 00:00:14,520
Are you even listening?

6
00:00:15,860 --> 00:00:17,500
Hello? You in there?

7
00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:18,380
Go home.

8
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:20,600
If anyone knows the answer, it's you.

9
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:21,780
Please go home.

10
00:00:21,960 --> 00:00:23,960
Why won't you just tell me what her favorite colors are?

11
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:26,860
Sawada, I am begging you.

12
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:29,360
You realize Valentine's Day is right around the corner

13
00:00:29,360 --> 00:00:32,020
and I can't wrap her present until I know which color we're going to use!

14
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:34,040
Don't ask her boyfriend about it, jeez!

15
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:37,600
It's important for a gift's wrapping to be as cute and appealing as possible.

16
00:00:38,060 --> 00:00:38,860
Don't you get it?

17
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:42,620
I know it looks nice, though it's not like I've dwelled on it.

18
00:00:43,280 --> 00:00:44,800
The art of gift wrap, huh?

19
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:47,420
Hold on a friggin' minute here.

20
00:00:48,260 --> 00:00:50,300
Are you planning to let the shop wrap your present?

21
00:00:51,980 --> 00:00:54,560
Well, what you choose doesn't involve me.

22
00:00:54,840 --> 00:00:57,280
But it's cute and appealing when they wrap it.

23
00:00:57,280 --> 00:00:59,640
Though I'm willing to learn your way as well.

24
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:00,060
Holly!

25
00:01:00,360 --> 00:01:02,420
I wish I knew which one to pick!

26
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:06,880
Red and orange are the colors I found Horimo's partial to.

27
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:08,400
See?

28
00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:09,940
That wasn't so hard now, right?

29
00:01:10,700 --> 00:01:10,980
Ooh!

30
00:01:11,340 --> 00:01:13,260
Check out this simple yet sweet wrapping here!

31
00:01:13,260 --> 00:01:17,300
キット知らないだろう

32
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:21,000
捨ててしまいたい過去

33
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,500
二人の助手だと

34
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:27,680
意味をくれたこと

35
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:31,900
キット知らないだろう

36
00:01:31,900 --> 00:01:35,260
キミが呼ぶ僕の名前

37
00:01:35,260 --> 00:01:42,260
キット知らないより大きな意味をくれたこと

38
00:01:42,260 --> 00:01:47,680
飲み干した甘いサイダー

39
00:01:47,680 --> 00:01:51,060
見せ返る僕を笑った

40
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:55,940
作った笑顔なんかも

41
00:01:55,940 --> 00:01:58,000
減らないね

42
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:00,000
どうしてどうして

43
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,000
どうして

44
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,000
もらって

45
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:06,000
中にいる僕を

46
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:10,000
愛しいというの

47
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,000
僕は何も

48
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:14,000
返して

49
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:15,000
返して

50
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:17,000
生きて

51
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:21,000
生きるんだろうが

52
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:25,000
眩しい思いが

53
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,000
満ちていく

54
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:32,000
この感情の

55
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:35,000
名前をそっと

56
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:39,000
キミに伝えよ

57
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,000
幸せ

58
00:02:42,000 --> 00:03:04,000
キャンヤン

59
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:08,000
キャンヤン

60
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,000
キャンヤン

61
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:14,000
キャンヤン

62
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:15,000
バガー

63
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:39,280
新た兄が

64
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:41,900
He'll be disappointed to get diddly-squat.

65
00:03:42,440 --> 00:03:45,360
Diddly is far better than my lousy sweets, I guarantee it.

66
00:03:45,820 --> 00:03:47,120
Well, in Remy's opinion,

67
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:49,360
he'd be happy to receive any gift from you.

68
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:55,340
She's underestimating how yucky that gift could be.

69
00:03:55,780 --> 00:03:56,260
10-4.

70
00:03:57,060 --> 00:03:57,920
What's up, you two?

71
00:03:58,040 --> 00:03:59,560
Oh, you know, just shoot in the breeze!

72
00:03:59,980 --> 00:04:01,520
You over here for class, or...?

73
00:04:01,520 --> 00:04:03,920
I had a little business to handle with me, I wanna...

74
00:04:03,920 --> 00:04:06,140
It's almost time, and I'm as ready as ever!

75
00:04:06,560 --> 00:04:08,140
This year, I'll pull out all the stops.

76
00:04:08,360 --> 00:04:09,080
What stops?

77
00:04:09,600 --> 00:04:11,980
Miyamura and I had a long talk about what kind of...

78
00:04:11,980 --> 00:04:13,060
Come on, Sawada!

79
00:04:13,220 --> 00:04:14,600
Don't wanna be late for class, right?

80
00:04:14,740 --> 00:04:15,300
Let's go!

81
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:16,700
I'll look like a total loser

82
00:04:16,700 --> 00:04:18,620
if she finds out I'm stressing over the gift grab!

83
00:04:19,240 --> 00:04:20,900
Any idea what that was about?

84
00:04:21,660 --> 00:04:22,100
None.

85
00:04:23,740 --> 00:04:24,180
Jeez!

86
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:26,940
Would it kill him to empathize with me just a little?

87
00:04:28,280 --> 00:04:30,420
That memory's gonna take me off for weeks!

88
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:32,100
Um, can we talk?

89
00:04:34,420 --> 00:04:35,360
I guess.

90
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:40,960
Aren't you, um, really good friends with some third-year students here?

91
00:04:42,580 --> 00:04:43,360
This again?

92
00:04:43,820 --> 00:04:44,860
I'd say so.

93
00:04:45,740 --> 00:04:46,860
But why are you asking?

94
00:04:47,700 --> 00:04:50,120
Well, Valentine's Day is coming up.

95
00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:50,700
Mm-hmm.

96
00:04:50,780 --> 00:04:51,920
And there's this guy.

97
00:04:52,380 --> 00:04:54,500
I'm almost positive he's one you hang out with.

98
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:59,120
Which one, though?

99
00:04:59,500 --> 00:05:01,600
Oh, um, thing is...

100
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:03,040
Is it Yanagi or Miyamura?

101
00:05:03,500 --> 00:05:05,160
Regardless, I can pass on your gift.

102
00:05:05,520 --> 00:05:07,720
Um, I don't know either of those boys.

103
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:08,660
Are these seniors?

104
00:05:08,660 --> 00:05:09,380
Huh?

105
00:05:13,060 --> 00:05:14,300
Is it Ishikawa?

106
00:05:15,220 --> 00:05:16,260
Maybe Sengoku?

107
00:05:16,640 --> 00:05:19,000
No, those names aren't ringing bells either.

108
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:20,300
They aren't?

109
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:23,500
Sorry, but he must be a third-year that I don't know.

110
00:05:24,080 --> 00:05:25,420
I think you do.

111
00:05:26,020 --> 00:05:28,880
He's the only person in your group who always wears a hoodie to school.

112
00:05:29,700 --> 00:05:31,720
Okay, Yura's your guy.

113
00:05:32,660 --> 00:05:34,660
Wait, that's who you met?!

114
00:05:34,660 --> 00:05:38,520
Oh, from the way you said that, I take it you have a thing for him?

115
00:05:38,700 --> 00:05:39,440
I'm sorry.

116
00:05:39,800 --> 00:05:44,240
There is zero romance between us, but, well, this mystery man is Yura?

117
00:05:45,060 --> 00:05:45,560
Mm-hmm.

118
00:05:47,780 --> 00:05:48,800
Is this a prank?

119
00:05:48,980 --> 00:05:49,720
It's not.

120
00:05:50,020 --> 00:05:52,100
He's so outgoing and energetic and...

121
00:05:52,100 --> 00:05:54,040
Oh gosh, I feel myself flushing.

122
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:58,400
He doesn't even know I exist since we haven't spoken a word to each other, but...

123
00:05:58,400 --> 00:06:02,440
Everybody loves getting a Valentine's treat and this is my last chance since he's about to graduate!

124
00:06:02,440 --> 00:06:02,700
Wait!

125
00:06:03,300 --> 00:06:04,980
Jeez, calm down, I get it.

126
00:06:05,180 --> 00:06:05,860
Deep breaths.

127
00:06:06,620 --> 00:06:08,840
I'm worried he won't accept it if he has a girlfriend.

128
00:06:09,840 --> 00:06:11,220
He doesn't, so don't.

129
00:06:11,300 --> 00:06:12,220
You sound pretty sure.

130
00:06:12,460 --> 00:06:13,800
What if they're keeping you low-key?

131
00:06:14,060 --> 00:06:14,780
There's no way.

132
00:06:15,140 --> 00:06:16,080
You should make a move.

133
00:06:16,540 --> 00:06:17,140
Ask him out.

134
00:06:17,540 --> 00:06:17,800
No!

135
00:06:18,060 --> 00:06:19,500
I just want to give him some chocolate.

136
00:06:19,940 --> 00:06:21,220
That's all it is.

137
00:06:21,420 --> 00:06:23,400
Dating him isn't my goal.

138
00:06:24,400 --> 00:06:24,800
Hmm.

139
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:27,760
This is great.

140
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:31,280
I've wanted to talk to someone about this for a while.

141
00:06:32,280 --> 00:06:34,500
None of our classmates would know who he is, though.

142
00:06:36,720 --> 00:06:39,120
Didn't think I'd get so flustered from saying it out loud.

143
00:06:40,080 --> 00:06:42,560
I'll listen if you need me to.

144
00:06:42,820 --> 00:06:45,400
You know, since I can't really help you out beyond that.

145
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:49,240
If it's okay, could you ask him what kind of chocolate he likes for me, please?

146
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:53,200
You really want to give some sugar without getting any back?

147
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:57,780
So you admire him from afar?

148
00:06:58,180 --> 00:06:58,580
Yes.

149
00:06:58,920 --> 00:07:00,020
That sounds about right.

150
00:07:00,700 --> 00:07:01,960
It's that time of year.

151
00:07:02,340 --> 00:07:05,100
Store shelves are going to be packed with Valentine's stuff everywhere.

152
00:07:05,580 --> 00:07:06,640
I feel you, man.

153
00:07:07,020 --> 00:07:10,140
But you're one of those guys who's going to be swimming in chocolate treats,

154
00:07:10,240 --> 00:07:11,460
so maybe I don't feel you.

155
00:07:11,900 --> 00:07:12,920
You already said you did.

156
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:13,780
No takebacks.

157
00:07:14,380 --> 00:07:16,980
So, any plans for the lovey-dovey day?

158
00:07:16,980 --> 00:07:18,920
Uh, practice tying a tie?

159
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:19,720
Yeah.

160
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:22,380
Is that what Miyamura's teaching you now?

161
00:07:22,520 --> 00:07:23,820
He said he wants to practice, too.

162
00:07:24,740 --> 00:07:25,140
Ta-da!

163
00:07:28,420 --> 00:07:30,560
No, it's not appealing at all.

164
00:07:30,740 --> 00:07:31,680
Yeah, you think?

165
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:35,100
I thought I tied it the way Sawada's magazine said to.

166
00:07:35,480 --> 00:07:36,960
What is this monstrosity?

167
00:07:37,220 --> 00:07:38,560
It's freaking tight, dude!

168
00:07:38,740 --> 00:07:40,120
I cannot tie your stupid knot!

169
00:07:40,740 --> 00:07:40,940
Huh?

170
00:07:41,280 --> 00:07:43,260
Hey, Sawada just showed up, guys.

171
00:07:44,020 --> 00:07:46,200
I'm guessing you came from Miyamura.

172
00:07:46,520 --> 00:07:46,960
No.

173
00:07:47,280 --> 00:07:48,180
Oh, hey, Sawada.

174
00:07:49,240 --> 00:07:52,900
I'm actually here for you, Iura.

175
00:07:53,120 --> 00:07:53,360
Me?

176
00:07:53,700 --> 00:07:54,000
Really?

177
00:07:54,300 --> 00:07:55,100
What's up, Dudette?

178
00:07:55,400 --> 00:07:58,840
Um, do you like chocolate or no?

179
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:01,840
Oh!

180
00:08:01,840 --> 00:08:05,060
G-could it be?

181
00:08:05,340 --> 00:08:06,920
I mean, it's gotta be.

182
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:08,740
Valentine's Day research!

183
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:10,620
Yes, I like chocolate.

184
00:08:10,960 --> 00:08:12,000
Do you have a favorite?

185
00:08:12,520 --> 00:08:13,340
I love them all.

186
00:08:13,840 --> 00:08:16,060
I'll be bitter or sweet, and I have no known allergies.

187
00:08:16,260 --> 00:08:16,440
Gay.

188
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:17,540
Hmm.

189
00:08:17,920 --> 00:08:20,640
Might as well sky-write how desperate you are, Shu.

190
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,900
So, yeah, any kind of chocolate works.

191
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:23,260
Got it.

192
00:08:23,380 --> 00:08:24,000
Thanks, Iura.

193
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:28,160
And he cut it off!

194
00:08:28,160 --> 00:08:28,360
Huh?

195
00:08:29,060 --> 00:08:31,260
You want to spend time and cash on chocolate for Shu?

196
00:08:31,260 --> 00:08:31,480
Wait.

197
00:08:31,980 --> 00:08:33,780
Shock someone besides Toadie is on your list.

198
00:08:33,820 --> 00:08:36,480
Shut your mouths right now before you discourage her, you killjoys!

199
00:08:36,680 --> 00:08:39,560
Hey, if you want to make me sweets, that's your prerogative, okay?

200
00:08:39,720 --> 00:08:39,940
Ugh.

201
00:08:39,940 --> 00:08:43,940
What kind of warped illusion did you invent to think I'd make sweets for you?

202
00:08:44,020 --> 00:08:44,420
Huh?

203
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:47,020
I'm going back to class.

204
00:08:47,940 --> 00:08:49,300
Where things make sense.

205
00:08:51,160 --> 00:08:51,560
Huh?

206
00:08:52,820 --> 00:08:53,260
What?

207
00:08:53,500 --> 00:08:54,940
She's the one who's not making sense, you know?

208
00:08:54,940 --> 00:08:56,680
Pilata is playing love games, my dude.

209
00:08:56,980 --> 00:08:58,620
I knew that wasn't what she was after.

210
00:08:59,020 --> 00:08:59,420
Chocolate!

211
00:09:02,740 --> 00:09:05,060
He said it doesn't matter what kind you get him.

212
00:09:05,480 --> 00:09:06,300
Works for me.

213
00:09:06,760 --> 00:09:09,360
That just means I have a lot of options and time to choose.

214
00:09:09,360 --> 00:09:11,420
It'd be easier if you narrowed it down.

215
00:09:11,940 --> 00:09:13,000
There are just so many.

216
00:09:13,920 --> 00:09:15,840
Thanks for coming to help me pick out something.

217
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:17,240
Don't sweat it.

218
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:20,860
I'm giving chocolates to someone special, too, so I wanted to see what they have.

219
00:09:21,300 --> 00:09:22,980
So you've also got someone special?

220
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:24,660
Oh, well, yes, but it's a secret.

221
00:09:24,820 --> 00:09:25,100
Aww.

222
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:36,560
If I can't give this to him, will you accept it instead?

223
00:09:36,940 --> 00:09:38,100
Don't worry, you'll do it.

224
00:09:38,100 --> 00:09:39,300
I know you will.

225
00:09:39,360 --> 00:09:42,260
I'll try my best.

226
00:09:48,820 --> 00:09:49,980
It's nearly here.

227
00:09:49,980 --> 00:10:01,740
Well, in Remy's humble opinion, he'd be happy to receive any gift from you.

228
00:10:01,740 --> 00:10:04,640
Okay.

229
00:10:07,580 --> 00:10:11,900
Um, what's a chocolate dessert that's so easy to make, not even a novice could botch it?

230
00:10:12,700 --> 00:10:13,100
Hmm.

231
00:10:13,100 --> 00:10:16,860
Oh, so you decided to make something for Miyamoto, then?

232
00:10:16,920 --> 00:10:17,160
Huh?

233
00:10:17,680 --> 00:10:19,460
The walls have ears and I don't want that chair!

234
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:22,220
We're the only ones in here and everyone knows you're dating.

235
00:10:22,220 --> 00:10:27,320
Miyamoto bakes, so I don't want him to find out I asked you instead.

236
00:10:27,320 --> 00:10:33,060
It won't be as pretty as the store-bought stuff, and I'm sure it's gonna be an acquired taste at best.

237
00:10:33,060 --> 00:10:41,900
But if there's anything I can't screw up entirely, am I really gonna give the simplest dessert on the planet to a cake shop owner's son?

238
00:10:41,900 --> 00:10:45,500
As simple as possible, but still delicious.

239
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:46,220
Hmm.

240
00:10:47,260 --> 00:10:48,360
I'll be right back.

241
00:10:48,360 --> 00:10:53,860
Whoa, too cool!

242
00:10:54,180 --> 00:10:55,460
Our school has recipe books?

243
00:10:55,680 --> 00:10:56,280
It does.

244
00:10:56,540 --> 00:10:58,980
And the ones in here are very easy to follow.

245
00:11:00,080 --> 00:11:03,700
I would check this book out on the regular when I started learning how to make desserts.

246
00:11:04,400 --> 00:11:06,380
Oh, chocolate desserts.

247
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:07,820
Ah, here it is.

248
00:11:08,620 --> 00:11:10,280
This one would be perfect for you.

249
00:11:10,820 --> 00:11:12,360
Kono's desserts are fantastic.

250
00:11:13,040 --> 00:11:14,720
But even she had to start somewhere.

251
00:11:14,720 --> 00:11:19,260
Here I go!

252
00:11:19,580 --> 00:11:22,040
Can I please eat this candy bar? I'm starving!

253
00:11:22,320 --> 00:11:23,120
Out, Kyousuke!

254
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:27,180
Let's try not to bother Kyoko when she's wielding weaponry, okay, honey?

255
00:11:27,440 --> 00:11:28,920
She's not preparing for war.

256
00:11:29,340 --> 00:11:29,700
Is she?

257
00:11:30,760 --> 00:11:32,100
What are you about to cook?

258
00:11:32,640 --> 00:11:33,800
Can we watch?

259
00:11:33,960 --> 00:11:36,660
I kinda need space, so you gotta watch from over there.

260
00:11:36,740 --> 00:11:37,960
Is it for anything special?

261
00:11:38,520 --> 00:11:39,960
Well, yeah, I guess so.

262
00:11:40,280 --> 00:11:42,560
It's, uh, Valentine's Day practice.

263
00:11:42,560 --> 00:11:45,640
It should be for Halloween since her face is so scary.

264
00:11:45,840 --> 00:11:47,100
Is she gonna fight her boyfriend?

265
00:11:47,300 --> 00:11:47,680
Hey!

266
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:49,700
Get out of here and let me concentrate!

267
00:11:49,960 --> 00:11:50,960
It's yours when it's done!

268
00:11:51,260 --> 00:11:51,700
Scary!

269
00:11:52,440 --> 00:11:52,700
Ah!

270
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:57,460
Of course I have a scary look.

271
00:11:58,260 --> 00:11:59,200
This is serious!

272
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:02,740
He may be happy no matter what,

273
00:12:02,880 --> 00:12:05,080
but he'll be happier if it tastes decent.

274
00:12:05,080 --> 00:12:16,860
It's not really good.

275
00:12:16,860 --> 00:12:17,300
Ugh!

276
00:12:17,920 --> 00:12:18,860
Um...

277
00:12:18,860 --> 00:12:20,100
Oh!

278
00:12:20,520 --> 00:12:21,580
Um, I see!

279
00:12:22,180 --> 00:12:23,220
Way to go, dummy!

280
00:12:23,460 --> 00:12:23,660
Huh?

281
00:12:24,040 --> 00:12:25,880
Uh, I'm here!

282
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:26,700
I'm gonna eat one!

283
00:12:26,780 --> 00:12:27,100
Yuna!

284
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:28,360
No, don't!

285
00:12:29,060 --> 00:12:30,500
Yeah, I'll try one, too!

286
00:12:31,020 --> 00:12:32,720
I'll go ahead and take one as well.

287
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:34,180
Please spare yourself!

288
00:12:34,260 --> 00:12:35,300
The stomach aches, everyone!

289
00:12:38,440 --> 00:12:39,720
It's not bad.

290
00:12:40,260 --> 00:12:41,680
I couldn't eat a bunch at once,

291
00:12:41,780 --> 00:12:42,500
but it's all right.

292
00:12:42,620 --> 00:12:43,840
It's edible, then?

293
00:12:45,960 --> 00:12:48,480
Kids like soda would never go for this.

294
00:12:48,660 --> 00:12:50,520
He might like bittersweet stuff when he's grown.

295
00:12:51,140 --> 00:12:52,420
I think they're perfect, though.

296
00:12:52,680 --> 00:12:53,660
So, more for me.

297
00:12:54,360 --> 00:12:56,400
Hey, that was the biggest piece on the plate, Yuri!

298
00:12:57,360 --> 00:12:58,600
So, it's good?

299
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:00,520
Depends on your taste!

300
00:13:00,640 --> 00:13:02,160
Just tell me whether it's good or not!

301
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:04,720
I don't know if it's good or not!

302
00:13:08,720 --> 00:13:10,700
Hori, please don't be so discouraged.

303
00:13:11,220 --> 00:13:13,420
I either like talent or taste or both.

304
00:13:13,740 --> 00:13:15,800
Self-deprecating thoughts like that won't help,

305
00:13:15,900 --> 00:13:16,800
so drop it now!

306
00:13:17,580 --> 00:13:17,980
Oh...

307
00:13:17,980 --> 00:13:21,220
In all honesty,

308
00:13:21,420 --> 00:13:23,060
I think you're worrying over nothing, Hori.

309
00:13:24,940 --> 00:13:25,940
Yes, it's bitter,

310
00:13:26,080 --> 00:13:28,380
but a lot of guys prefer not-so-sweet sweets.

311
00:13:28,820 --> 00:13:30,340
Look, I can handle the truth!

312
00:13:30,340 --> 00:13:33,260
I promise I won't rage if you tell it to me straight!

313
00:13:33,340 --> 00:13:35,140
You're already getting hysterical, though!

314
00:13:35,780 --> 00:13:36,460
They're awful.

315
00:13:36,920 --> 00:13:38,740
From the taste to the lumpy shape.

316
00:13:38,740 --> 00:13:42,780
Hey, remember what Remy said?

317
00:13:43,260 --> 00:13:43,460
Huh?

318
00:13:44,260 --> 00:13:45,740
Miyamura will be over the moon

319
00:13:45,740 --> 00:13:47,940
to receive any present you make for him, right?

320
00:13:49,520 --> 00:13:51,300
Store-bought stuff might look prettier

321
00:13:51,300 --> 00:13:53,200
and have a taste a lot of people love,

322
00:13:53,300 --> 00:13:55,360
but that's not what matters with most gifts.

323
00:13:56,120 --> 00:13:56,640
Besides,

324
00:13:57,140 --> 00:13:58,520
I really like yours!

325
00:13:58,740 --> 00:13:59,220
Know why?

326
00:13:59,220 --> 00:14:01,220
It reminds me of you.

327
00:14:04,480 --> 00:14:05,300
Oh, no!

328
00:14:05,720 --> 00:14:06,460
I was, um,

329
00:14:06,700 --> 00:14:08,000
not expecting a back hug!

330
00:14:09,200 --> 00:14:09,940
She's right.

331
00:14:10,220 --> 00:14:13,220
What matters most when it comes to gifts is...

332
00:14:13,920 --> 00:14:15,860
Happy Valentine's Day!

333
00:14:16,200 --> 00:14:17,440
You're gonna make me blush.

334
00:14:17,800 --> 00:14:18,820
I feel special.

335
00:14:18,980 --> 00:14:19,280
What?

336
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:20,560
They aren't romantic sweets.

337
00:14:20,800 --> 00:14:21,780
I figured that.

338
00:14:22,300 --> 00:14:23,300
No harm done.

339
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:23,680
Hey!

340
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:24,820
Yuda!

341
00:14:25,520 --> 00:14:27,180
Your obligatory chocolate, sir.

342
00:14:27,180 --> 00:14:29,080
Can't you at least call it friendship chocolate?

343
00:14:29,440 --> 00:14:29,800
Ooh!

344
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:31,380
The Miyamura cake shop brand.

345
00:14:31,520 --> 00:14:33,060
The Ayori cake shop brand.

346
00:14:33,500 --> 00:14:35,020
There isn't a girl in school

347
00:14:35,020 --> 00:14:36,440
who brought more chocolate than him.

348
00:14:36,940 --> 00:14:37,860
This is true.

349
00:14:38,900 --> 00:14:39,420
How do you wait?

350
00:14:40,520 --> 00:14:41,740
Can you come over today?

351
00:14:42,220 --> 00:14:43,040
I'll work it in.

352
00:14:43,500 --> 00:14:44,820
Would right after school be good?

353
00:14:45,240 --> 00:14:45,940
Yeah, okay.

354
00:14:46,740 --> 00:14:47,520
Then again,

355
00:14:47,740 --> 00:14:49,560
I need a little time before you get there,

356
00:14:49,660 --> 00:14:50,680
so just walk slow.

357
00:14:51,040 --> 00:14:51,820
In that case,

358
00:14:51,820 --> 00:14:53,160
I'll stop by my place first.

359
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:55,660
If you feel like it's too dark before you head out,

360
00:14:56,280 --> 00:14:57,160
Colin, I'll come get you.

361
00:14:57,500 --> 00:14:58,180
I'll be fine.

362
00:14:58,760 --> 00:14:59,640
Then I'll see you later.

363
00:15:01,260 --> 00:15:02,700
Must have to prep his gift.

364
00:15:03,280 --> 00:15:04,980
I thought it'd just be homemade sweets,

365
00:15:05,140 --> 00:15:06,380
but he didn't bring it to school

366
00:15:06,380 --> 00:15:08,480
and apparently can't bring it to my house.

367
00:15:10,420 --> 00:15:11,720
How big is this thing?

368
00:15:12,500 --> 00:15:13,160
What is it?

369
00:15:13,560 --> 00:15:14,800
I'm dying to know!

370
00:15:15,360 --> 00:15:16,440
Bodhi-senpai!

371
00:15:17,560 --> 00:15:19,160
Happy Valentine's Day!

372
00:15:19,680 --> 00:15:21,300
I made this gift just for you!

373
00:15:21,460 --> 00:15:23,420
It's full of my hard work and love!

374
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:24,720
Thank you, but you shouldn't have.

375
00:15:25,100 --> 00:15:26,940
This is what she pulled out all the stops for.

376
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:28,440
Aww!

377
00:15:29,100 --> 00:15:30,000
It's so cute!

378
00:15:30,060 --> 00:15:30,980
I'm glad you like it!

379
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:31,900
Really glad!

380
00:15:32,360 --> 00:15:34,480
This darling little bow is a great color.

381
00:15:35,140 --> 00:15:36,920
I'm almost sad to untie it.

382
00:15:37,920 --> 00:15:39,220
Miyamura knows you best.

383
00:15:39,780 --> 00:15:40,960
He said you like orange.

384
00:15:40,960 --> 00:15:45,300
I can't even begin to describe how annoying it was to get help from him,

385
00:15:45,420 --> 00:15:48,280
but he was positive that one would make you smile.

386
00:15:49,420 --> 00:15:51,700
He knew it'd make me smile.

387
00:15:51,700 --> 00:15:57,000
I love it!

388
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:58,080
Thank you!

389
00:15:58,080 --> 00:16:03,760
Maybe seeing someone you like with a big, goofy grin on their face

390
00:16:03,760 --> 00:16:06,080
is what today is really all about.

391
00:16:06,080 --> 00:16:07,080
Good!

392
00:16:09,540 --> 00:16:10,360
Both of you are here!

393
00:16:10,540 --> 00:16:11,280
Special delivery!

394
00:16:12,240 --> 00:16:12,900
What is it?

395
00:16:13,400 --> 00:16:14,820
We'll call it a choco-gram.

396
00:16:15,040 --> 00:16:17,160
I'm giving them to everyone so they're kind of tiny,

397
00:16:17,420 --> 00:16:19,320
but they're a lot better than last year's batch.

398
00:16:19,320 --> 00:16:20,040
Oh, wow!

399
00:16:22,980 --> 00:16:24,900
I'll save it for when I get home, okay?

400
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:26,460
Yes, so will I!

401
00:16:26,520 --> 00:16:27,440
Don't wait too long!

402
00:16:27,960 --> 00:16:28,420
Bye!

403
00:16:29,580 --> 00:16:31,400
It's like a storm blew through here.

404
00:16:35,140 --> 00:16:35,500
Yoshikawa!

405
00:16:35,500 --> 00:16:38,620
You called?

406
00:16:38,840 --> 00:16:40,660
I also have a special delivery thing.

407
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:41,820
Here.

408
00:16:44,720 --> 00:16:46,760
Oh, I'll make sure it gets to him.

409
00:16:46,860 --> 00:16:48,000
I appreciate it, but, um,

410
00:16:49,080 --> 00:16:50,720
look inside first, okay?

411
00:16:51,220 --> 00:16:51,660
What?

412
00:16:51,860 --> 00:16:52,220
See ya.

413
00:16:54,160 --> 00:16:56,120
She wants me to see his gift?

414
00:16:57,040 --> 00:16:58,280
Guess she got him too.

415
00:16:58,280 --> 00:16:58,420
Huh?

416
00:17:05,500 --> 00:17:19,700
I'm not too early, am I?

417
00:17:20,380 --> 00:17:21,220
Hope not.

418
00:17:21,680 --> 00:17:23,280
Believe it or not, you're right on time.

419
00:17:23,840 --> 00:17:24,480
Have a seat.

420
00:17:25,180 --> 00:17:25,860
Where's your mom?

421
00:17:26,580 --> 00:17:27,780
She should be home soon.

422
00:17:28,340 --> 00:17:28,640
Uh-huh.

423
00:17:33,220 --> 00:17:35,020
I wonder if he'll like his chocolate.

424
00:17:35,500 --> 00:17:39,300
He's nice to a fault,

425
00:17:39,500 --> 00:17:41,020
so he'll probably say it's awesome

426
00:17:41,020 --> 00:17:42,220
even if he wants to gag.

427
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:45,340
Thanks for waiting.

428
00:17:46,700 --> 00:17:47,360
Mi amor-

429
00:17:47,360 --> 00:17:52,540
Happy Valentine's Day.

430
00:17:54,040 --> 00:17:56,400
I thought I'd go with a classic Valentine cake.

431
00:17:57,060 --> 00:17:58,360
It smells so good!

432
00:17:58,720 --> 00:18:00,700
You don't mind if I go ahead and dig in, do you?

433
00:18:01,200 --> 00:18:01,640
Thanks!

434
00:18:03,640 --> 00:18:03,920
Oh.

435
00:18:05,500 --> 00:18:07,980
Delicious as always.

436
00:18:09,180 --> 00:18:11,660
I was kind of holding my breath for a hot minute there.

437
00:18:11,860 --> 00:18:13,940
You were honestly worried I wouldn't like your cake?

438
00:18:14,300 --> 00:18:16,720
Well, uh, the cake itself wasn't what worried me.

439
00:18:17,300 --> 00:18:18,220
The gift wrap, though.

440
00:18:18,400 --> 00:18:20,240
As you see, I struggled to figure that out.

441
00:18:21,140 --> 00:18:22,700
If it hadn't looked nice enough,

442
00:18:22,760 --> 00:18:23,900
I would have brought it to your house.

443
00:18:24,320 --> 00:18:24,520
Hmm?

444
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:27,540
Sorry it's not fancier, despite this being a special day.

445
00:18:27,540 --> 00:18:34,100
I didn't even think to gift wrap my stinking homemade chocolate.

446
00:18:34,480 --> 00:18:35,360
Fancy-schmancy!

447
00:18:35,560 --> 00:18:36,260
This is great!

448
00:18:36,380 --> 00:18:37,000
I love it!

449
00:18:37,360 --> 00:18:38,280
What a relief.

450
00:18:38,660 --> 00:18:40,280
Well, I can't fix it now.

451
00:18:41,360 --> 00:18:42,700
I also made you something,

452
00:18:43,060 --> 00:18:44,300
since we're Valentine's and all.

453
00:18:44,560 --> 00:18:44,940
Oh.

454
00:18:45,220 --> 00:18:46,680
I wondered what that bag was for.

455
00:18:46,860 --> 00:18:47,220
Yes.

456
00:18:47,440 --> 00:18:48,660
Well, as I'm sure you know,

457
00:18:48,700 --> 00:18:49,900
it's inferior to your baking.

458
00:18:50,160 --> 00:18:51,340
Your stomach may spite you.

459
00:18:51,340 --> 00:18:52,740
Don't diss your own gift.

460
00:18:54,140 --> 00:18:54,660
Oh.

461
00:18:55,420 --> 00:18:56,820
Chocolate ganache squares?

462
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:58,020
I love ganache.

463
00:18:58,360 --> 00:18:59,440
I'm such a dummy.

464
00:18:59,980 --> 00:19:01,600
Making gifts with care is one thing,

465
00:19:01,700 --> 00:19:03,620
but wrapping them with care completes the gesture.

466
00:19:04,480 --> 00:19:07,180
I was too focused on taste to fret about presentation.

467
00:19:08,240 --> 00:19:09,820
Oh, this plate's from your house.

468
00:19:10,840 --> 00:19:12,000
Kind of comforts me.

469
00:19:13,740 --> 00:19:14,180
Huh?

470
00:19:14,820 --> 00:19:16,060
He's really chowing down.

471
00:19:16,820 --> 00:19:17,620
Are they good?

472
00:19:18,080 --> 00:19:18,980
They're very good.

473
00:19:19,320 --> 00:19:20,260
Just sweet enough.

474
00:19:21,340 --> 00:19:22,840
Here, try one before I inhale them.

475
00:19:23,600 --> 00:19:24,140
Say, ah.

476
00:19:27,140 --> 00:19:28,360
It's tasty, right?

477
00:19:28,740 --> 00:19:29,820
I guess so.

478
00:19:30,740 --> 00:19:31,840
Beats the practice batch.

479
00:19:32,400 --> 00:19:33,280
By a long shot.

480
00:19:34,120 --> 00:19:36,480
Hard to relax till you see how your partner reacts.

481
00:19:37,220 --> 00:19:37,460
Huh?

482
00:19:38,740 --> 00:19:39,220
Hmm?

483
00:19:40,460 --> 00:19:42,240
He felt the same way I did.

484
00:19:43,340 --> 00:19:44,200
How's the cake?

485
00:19:44,640 --> 00:19:45,260
Do you approve?

486
00:19:45,520 --> 00:19:45,880
What?

487
00:19:46,180 --> 00:19:47,600
Everything you make is delicious.

488
00:19:47,860 --> 00:19:48,920
Of course I approve.

489
00:19:49,820 --> 00:19:50,880
You had another relief.

490
00:19:51,340 --> 00:19:56,100
How am I supposed to eat with you staring at me?

491
00:19:56,580 --> 00:19:57,660
Oh, I'm sorry.

492
00:19:58,400 --> 00:20:00,740
Chocolate cake that simply melts in your mouth.

493
00:20:01,500 --> 00:20:03,220
Whipped cream that isn't too sweet.

494
00:20:04,180 --> 00:20:05,400
Just how I like it.

495
00:20:05,900 --> 00:20:07,560
Now what should I make next here?

496
00:20:07,860 --> 00:20:08,300
Stop!

497
00:20:08,440 --> 00:20:09,000
Too soon!

498
00:20:09,080 --> 00:20:11,700
You're gonna eat it, right?

499
00:20:11,700 --> 00:20:15,240
Do you even have to ask?

500
00:20:15,960 --> 00:20:18,540
It's something that only I'll get to taste.

501
00:20:19,580 --> 00:20:21,420
Have you thought about what you're gonna make for me?

502
00:20:22,080 --> 00:20:24,040
This is gonna be hard to top.

503
00:20:24,580 --> 00:20:27,260
I like his word and cute as you did today and it'll be a win.

504
00:20:27,540 --> 00:20:28,940
AVERT YOUR EYES!

505
00:20:28,940 --> 00:20:30,360
I can't look at your face!

506
00:20:31,360 --> 00:20:35,520
He put his whole heart into that cake and it tasted like happiness.

507
00:20:35,520 --> 00:20:37,380
I like it.

508
00:20:37,480 --> 00:20:39,760
The cake and the cake and have mindfulness.

509
00:20:39,760 --> 00:21:09,740
Thank you.

510
00:21:09,760 --> 00:21:39,740
Thank you.

511
00:21:39,760 --> 00:22:09,740
Thank you.

512
00:22:09,760 --> 00:22:13,460
Oh, hi, Sawada.

513
00:22:15,640 --> 00:22:17,860
All the seniors are leaving soon.

514
00:22:19,060 --> 00:22:19,580
I know.

515
00:22:19,580 --> 00:22:22,640
I can't do it.

516
00:22:22,920 --> 00:22:25,480
Should have known since I can't even talk to the boys in class.

517
00:22:25,960 --> 00:22:27,640
What an awful excuse that is, right?

518
00:22:27,640 --> 00:22:30,140
I'm sorry.

519
00:22:30,820 --> 00:22:33,180
You were such a huge help, but it was all for nothing.

520
00:22:34,320 --> 00:22:35,880
Hey, I can go give it to him.

521
00:22:37,160 --> 00:22:38,600
That's not the issue here.

522
00:22:38,600 --> 00:22:43,100
She wanted to give it to him herself.

523
00:22:44,100 --> 00:22:46,020
What a waste of perfectly good chocolate.

524
00:22:46,700 --> 00:22:48,700
But at least a shopping trip is a nice memory.

525
00:22:50,080 --> 00:22:50,840
Thank you.

526
00:22:51,840 --> 00:22:52,280
Wait.

527
00:22:53,320 --> 00:22:54,800
Then let me have the chocolate.

528
00:22:54,800 --> 00:22:58,100
But you said I could have it if you didn't give it to him.

529
00:22:58,440 --> 00:22:59,880
That way it won't go to waste.

530
00:23:00,540 --> 00:23:01,440
I'll eat all of it.

531
00:23:02,900 --> 00:23:03,300
Really?

532
00:23:03,300 --> 00:23:06,700
Even if you hate the flavor?

533
00:23:09,200 --> 00:23:09,640
Okay.

534
00:23:11,400 --> 00:23:12,260
It's yours.

535
00:23:12,520 --> 00:23:12,860
Thanks.

536
00:23:14,300 --> 00:23:14,600
Here.

537
00:23:14,960 --> 00:23:15,360
Trade ya.

538
00:23:16,160 --> 00:23:17,260
I got it yesterday.

539
00:23:18,060 --> 00:23:18,580
For you.

540
00:23:18,580 --> 00:23:21,640
What do they call these gifts?

541
00:23:22,280 --> 00:23:22,920
Obligatory?

542
00:23:23,280 --> 00:23:23,720
Or whatever?

543
00:23:24,820 --> 00:23:26,940
I really appreciate this.

544
00:23:27,580 --> 00:23:30,300
It isn't some obligatory chocolate, though.

545
00:23:30,700 --> 00:23:32,080
It's friendship chocolate.

546
00:23:32,080 --> 00:23:32,180
I'm sorry.

